/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL003-M3 -- turbulent pipe, steady simpleFoam + wall-RESOLVED kOmegaSST.

  ONE registered numerics change vs VMFL003-M2 ARM D, and it is an INSTRUMENT
  fix, never a physics lever (VERIFICATION_CHARTER section 2ay: "if it's the
  numerics, change the numerics"):

      p solver:  GAMG (GaussSeidel)  ->  PCG with DIC preconditioner

  WHY, and it is MEASURED, not a precaution.  The wall-resolved radial mesh has
  a near-wall cell aspect ratio of 204 (L1) to 817 (L3).  In an answer-blind
  scratch smoke (y+ and linear-solver iteration counts read; Delta p NEVER
  read), GAMG+GaussSeidel hit its 1000-iteration ceiling EVERY outer SIMPLE step
  on the aspect-409 mesh -- it does not converge the pressure equation on
  high-aspect cells -- which would make the graded run ~1000x too slow and blow
  the compute budget (CLAUDE.md rule 12).  PCG with the DIC preconditioner
  solved the same pressure equation in 0-1 inner iterations per step and drove
  the outer residuals of p, Ux, k and omega down monotonically.  DIC-
  preconditioned CG is the standard robust choice for the ill-conditioned
  pressure matrix of a high-aspect-ratio boundary-layer mesh.

  This touches NEITHER the gate (Delta p band, Colebrook diagnostic) NOR the
  frozen iterative-convergence RESIDUAL floor RESID_TOL = 1e-8, which is carried
  BYTE-IDENTICAL from M2 and is NOT relaxed.  The linear-solver tolerances below
  govern how well each equation is solved PER outer iteration; the verdict-
  determining quantity is the FINAL INITIAL residual of the outer SIMPLE loop,
  read by the comparator after the run.

  NO residualControl: the run ALWAYS reaches endTime, so rule 4's clauses
  "last time == endTime" and "ExecutionTime count == endTime" are meaningful.
  Iterative convergence is judged AFTER the run, PER LEVEL and BEFORE the Roache
  triple is formed (CLAUDE.md rule 5 step 1), from BOTH the final initial
  residuals AND the plateau of the gate quantity.

  EVERY VARIABLE simpleFoam+kOmegaSST SOLVES HAS AN ENTRY: p and U (simpleFoam),
  k and omega (kOmegaSST); nut is algebraic.  The regex "(U|k|omega)" covers all
  transported variables as a CLASS (the L-221/L-222 posture: fix the class, not
  the instance).  The domain is OPEN, so the pressure level is pinned by the
  outlet BC and NO pRefCell/pRefValue is set.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      fvSolution;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

solvers
{
    p
    {
        solver          PCG;
        preconditioner  DIC;
        tolerance       1e-12;
        relTol          0.01;
    }

    "(U|k|omega)"
    {
        solver          smoothSolver;
        smoother        symGaussSeidel;
        tolerance       1e-13;
        relTol          0.01;
    }
}

SIMPLE
{
    nNonOrthogonalCorrectors 1;
    consistent      no;
    residualControl
    {
    }
}

relaxationFactors
{
    equations
    {
        U               0.7;
        k               0.7;
        omega           0.7;
    }
    fields
    {
        p               0.3;
    }
}

// ************************************************************************* //
